{
  "files": [
    {
      "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <math.h>\n\n#define N_ITER 10 // number of simulation iterations\n#define DT 0.01f // time step\n#define SOFTENING 1e-9f // to avoid zero divisors\n\ntypedef struct { float x, y, z, vx, vy, vz; } Body;\n\nvoid body_force(const float * restrict x,\n                const float * restrict y,\n                const float * restrict z,\n                float * restrict vx,\n                float * restrict vy,\n                float * restrict vz,\n                float dt, int n) {\n#pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\n  for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n    float xi = x[i];\n    float yi = y[i];\n    float zi = z[i];\n    float fx = 0.0f;\n    float fy = 0.0f;\n    float fz = 0.0f;\n\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n      float dx = x[j] - xi;\n      float dy = y[j] - yi;\n      float dz = z[j] - zi;\n      float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\n      float inv_dist = 1.0f / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\n      float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\n\n      fx += dx * inv_dist3;\n      fy += dy * inv_dist3;\n      fz += dz * inv_dist3;\n    }\n\n    vx[i] += dt*fx;\n    vy[i] += dt*fy;\n    vz[i] += dt*fz;\n  }\n}\n\nBody* read_dataset(int *nbodies) {\n  int b = fread(nbodies, sizeof(*nbodies), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading nbodie value\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n  Body *bodies = (Body *)malloc(*nbodies * sizeof(Body));\n  b = fread(bodies, *nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading input values\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n  return bodies;\n}\n\nvoid write_dataset(const int nbodies, Body *bodies) {\n  int b = fwrite(bodies, nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdout);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError writing to output\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n}\n\nint main(int argc,char **argv) {\n  int nbodies;\n  Body *bodies = read_dataset(&nbodies);\n\n  // Convert to structure-of-arrays for better cache locality.\n  float *x = (float *)malloc(nbodies * sizeof(float));\n  float *y = (float *)malloc(nbodies * sizeof(float));\n  float *z = (float *)malloc(nbodies * sizeof(float));\n  float *vx = (float *)malloc(nbodies * sizeof(float));\n  float *vy = (float *)malloc(nbodies * sizeof(float));\n  float *vz = (float *)malloc(nbodies * sizeof(float));\n\n  for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n    x[i] = bodies[i].x;\n    y[i] = bodies[i].y;\n    z[i] = bodies[i].z;\n    vx[i] = bodies[i].vx;\n    vy[i] = bodies[i].vy;\n    vz[i] = bodies[i].vz;\n  }\n\n  for (int iter = 0; iter < N_ITER; ++iter) {\n    body_force(x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, DT, nbodies);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n      x[i] += vx[i] * DT;\n      y[i] += vy[i] * DT;\n      z[i] += vz[i] * DT;\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Pack back into the original layout for output.\n  for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n    bodies[i].x = x[i];\n    bodies[i].y = y[i];\n    bodies[i].z = z[i];\n    bodies[i].vx = vx[i];\n    bodies[i].vy = vy[i];\n    bodies[i].vz = vz[i];\n  }\n\n  write_dataset(nbodies, bodies);\n\n  free(x); free(y); free(z);\n  free(vx); free(vy); free(vz);\n  free(bodies);\n\n  exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);\n}\n",
      "path": "src/nbody.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Converting the body data from an array-of-structs to a structure-of-arrays layout improves cache line utilization because each inner-loop pass reads only the position components (x, y, z) as three sequential streams instead of loading unused velocity fields. Parallelizing the i-loop with OpenMP static scheduling distributes independent per-body force accumulations across 4 cores while preserving the exact j-order summation for bit-identical output.",
  "notes": "The arithmetic order inside each i iteration is unchanged (j from 0 to n-1, same operations), so floating-point results are identical to the sequential reference. The SoA conversion and packing are O(n) overheads negligible against the O(n^2) force computation. restrict pointers help the compiler disambiguate memory accesses.",
  "sources_kept": [],
  "transformations": [
    "Change data layout from AoS (Body struct array) to SoA (separate x,y,z,vx,vy,vz arrays)",
    "Parallelize body_force i-loop with OpenMP static scheduling",
    "Add restrict qualifiers to force computation parameters"
  ]
